Subject: [PATCH 1/5] Drop TorchScript where kornia calls cannot be scripted

torch.jit.script fails to compile kornia.filters calls on current torch/kornia.
pyrdown and NormalGenerator run as plain Python; behaviour is unchanged.
---
 utils/generic_utils.py  | 1 -
 utils/geometry_utils.py | 5 ++---
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/utils/generic_utils.py b/utils/generic_utils.py
index 339ad4a..efbb571 100644
--- a/utils/generic_utils.py
+++ b/utils/generic_utils.py
@@ -84,7 +84,6 @@ def normalize_depth(depth_b1hw: torch.Tensor,
     return torch.cat(depths_norm_11hw, dim=0)
 
 
-@torch.jit.script
 def pyrdown(input_tensor: torch.Tensor, num_scales: int = 4):
     """ Creates a downscale pyramid for the input tensor. """
     output = [input_tensor]
